SADC FREIGHTLINK Payment Engine Specification v2.0
Objective

The Payment Engine is responsible for calculating, managing, and tracking the complete financial lifecycle of every customer booking, from booking creation until the invoice is fully settled.

The engine must support:

Payment at Booking (PAB)
Cash on Delivery (COD)
Credit Accounts
NET Payment Terms
Statement-based payments
POD-based payments
Invoice-based payments
Enterprise Accounts Payable workflows
Future ERP integrations

The Payment Engine must never hardcode payment dates. Instead, it calculates payment schedules from the client's configured Financial Account.

Payment Types

The first decision the engine makes is:

How is this booking being paid?

Supported payment types:

Payment Type	Description
Payment at Booking (PAB)	Customer pays immediately before booking is confirmed.
Instant EFT	Immediate electronic payment.
Credit / Debit Card	Immediate payment through payment gateway.
Cash on Delivery (COD)	Customer pays after delivery before POD is released or according to agreed COD workflow.
Credit Account	Customer has approved credit terms.
Contract Account	Dedicated lane or contract billing.
Engine Decision Tree

Every booking follows this workflow.

Booking Created
        │
        ▼
Determine Payment Type
        │
        ├── PAB
        │      │
        │      ▼
        │ Process Payment
        │
        ├── COD
        │      │
        │      ▼
        │ Wait For Delivery
        │
        └── Credit Account
               │
               ▼
Read Financial Account
               │
               ▼
Calculate Payment Schedule
               │
               ▼
Create Invoice
