Cash on Delivery (COD)

COD is also separate.

Workflow

Booking Created

↓

Shipment Delivered

↓

Await Customer Payment

↓

Payment Received

↓

Invoice Settled

↓

Release POD

The platform should allow configurable COD rules, because some customers pay:

Immediately upon delivery.
Before the POD is released.
Within a short agreed period after delivery.
Financial Dates Stored Per Shipment

Every shipment should store:

Booking Date

Pickup Date

Delivery Date

Invoice Date

POD Uploaded Date

POD Approved Date

Statement Date

Payment Trigger Date

Due Date

Expected Payment Date

Actual Payment Date

These dates are calculated once and persisted for reporting and cash-flow forecasting.

Financial Account Responsibilities

The Financial Account becomes the source of truth for payment behaviour.

It answers:

What payment type does this customer use?
What starts the payment countdown?
Is a statement required?
What is the statement cycle?
What are the statement cut-off dates?
Are PODs required?
What documents are required?
What happens if the cut-off is missed?
What are the payment terms?
What is the payment run schedule?

The Payment Engine reads these settings and applies them uniformly to every shipment, eliminating client-specific logic from the codebase.